From e517358c24144c514b0516ad16398d83b54276d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elton Wang <elton.wang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 01:01:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: use configurable error retry delay

When an NVMe device enters the error state, the sensor of the device
is skipped for `scanDelayTicks` poll cycles. Currently `scanDelayTicks`
is hardcoded to 300 ticks, about 5 minutes at the one second poll
interval.

Recovery time varies between devices, so changing the hardcoded value
cannot suit every platform.

Support configuring `scanDelayTicks` via the `ErrorRetryDelay`
property [1] of each sensor configuration, so a device can be given a
delay matching its own recovery time. When the property is absent the
current 300 ticks are used, so existing configurations are unaffected.

[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/94231

Tested:
1. Set `ErrorRetryDelay` to 5 for RIO_GRANDE_SSD_0_TEMP_C, then
   confirmed the sensor is retried every 5 poll cycles instead of every
   300.
   - Powered the SSD off with the host still running. After 5 failed
     attempts the sensor fell into the error state and was marked
     unavailable. The sensor was retried every 5 seconds.
